WYOMING:
Section1.DEFINITIONS.
CITY EMPLOYEE/EMPLOYEES.Employee or employees as usedin this ordinance
means civilian City employees, but does not include the sworn personnel of the Cheyenne Police
Department below the rankof chief or the sworn personnel of the Cheyenne Fire Department
below the rank of chief.
Section.2.APPLICABILITY.
These terms and conditions of employment apply to all City employees.
Section3.PURPOSE.
The purpose of this ordinance is to define the terms and conditions of employment for City
employees. In areas of conflict between this ordinance and established federal, state or local laws,
the latter shall govern.This ordinance comprises the exclusive statement of City employee terms
by a supervisor, agent or officer of the City of Cheyenne whichis in conflict with orin addition to
this ordinance is specifically disclaimed bythe City of Cheyenne, except for the City of Cheyenne
Personnel Rules and Regulations effective February 17, 2015 ("Personnel Rules and
Regulations"), policies promulgated by the mayor pursuant to Chapter IIl, Section 1 of the
personnel and employees establishing specific job expectations, requirements or discipline which
are part of the employee's official personnel file maintained by the Human Resources Department.
Section4.COMPENSATION.
The compensation paid to employees will be based on current market salary data utilized
by the Human Resources Department to determine equitable and justwages.The governing body
reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to modify orchange pay scales.
Effeetive July 1, 2008,
City employees will-reeeive, in addition to basie pay, longevity pay as set forth in Exhibit A,
